@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Integration via Details
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account information transfers properly to the account details page.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Vchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Pchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Onepro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the fourth default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the fifth default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Vchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Pchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| VCHILDVCHILD |
	| PCHILDPCHILD |
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| VCHILDVCHILD |
	| PCHILDPCHILD |
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Vchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Pchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId4}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId5}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View T4 project
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and viewing the project in the provisioning page account details 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "PROKORKORPRO" should be part of the support site
	When I assign the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I create a team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following account values in the account details page
	| Name           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | PROKORKORPRO                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| Country        | United States                 |
	| SLA            | Platinum                      |
	| Support Seats  | 1 / 3 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T4                            |
	| FLS Partner    | Koroneiki Partner             |
	When I click on the "Details" tab
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Account Name        | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| State               | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Code                | PROKORKORPRO                  | |
	| Tier                | T4                            | |
	| Parent              | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |	|
	| Data Region         | United States                 | |
	| First Line Support  | Koroneiki Partner             |	|
	| Liferay Version     | DXP 7.1                       | |
	| Street 1            | 456 Fake Street               | |
	| Country             | United States                 | |
	| City                | Diamond Bar                   | |
	| State/Province      | California                    | |
	| Postal Code         | 91765                         | |
	| Primary             | true                          | |
	| Dossiera Project    | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}   | |
	| Salesforce Project  | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | |
	When I click on the "Support" tab
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Support Region   | United States | |
	| Support Language | English       | |
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "contactEmailAddress" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account                 |
	| Update Field Name           | contactEmailAddress                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "internal" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | internal             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | false                |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "code" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | code                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | PROKORKORPRO         |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "region" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | region               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | United States        |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "liferayVersion" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
    | Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
    | Update Field Name           | liferayVersion       |
    | Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
    | Update Field New Value      | DXP 7.1              |
	And I generate the account ID value for "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "parentAccountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | parentAccountId      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}   |
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}   |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "name" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account          |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | status               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | Active               |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "tier" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | tier                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | T4                   |

